+`E2B_MAX_STARTING_INSTANCES_PER_NODE` supplies the positive-integer fallback for
+`max-starting-instances-per-node` (upstream default 3). It controls concurrent
+start/resume operations independently of the running-instance quota. The environment
+value is read when the process starts; a configured LaunchDarkly value still wins,
+and the orchestrator refreshes the resulting semaphore limit every 30 seconds.
